lines+=['','## Stock strictFunctionTypes and declaration experiments','','All ledgers use the actual **stock tsc 6.0.3 CLI**, the 79-root compiler tsconfig and explicit `--strictFunctionTypes true --noEmit --incremental false --composite false --pretty false --noErrorTruncation`. The checkout’s node types resolve normally. [root-manifest.json](evidence/root-manifest.json) records the roots/options; [baseline](evidence/strict-baseline.json), [property](evidence/strict-properties.json) and [hybrid](evidence/strict-hybrid.json) retain the complete diagnostics. Earlier missing-node prototype diagnostics are discarded.','','The property road converts **53 unique source member groups across 5 files** for the 11 receiver types, including inherited declarations; overloads become callable property type literals. Transpiling every changed file with stock TypeScript, ES2020/ESNext and comments removed produced byte-identical JavaScript. The hybrid converts **16 internal/private groups**, and replaces the 19 public patterns with 82 receiver arrows. Original callable types are restored locally with type assertions to preserve generics and overloads; optional undefined values, defaults and printer identity guards are preserved. These choices are part of the measured recipe, not a claim that Adamic supports every introduced syntax form.','','The exact private recipes are [properties-source.patch](properties-source.patch), [hybrid-source.patch](hybrid-source.patch) and [variants.cjs](variants.cjs). A fresh typed scan found **baseline 29, property road 0, hybrid 0** method-signature object-binding sites. [road-audit.json](evidence/road-audit.json) also records source internal-tag ownership.','','The property road’s sole diagnostic is:','','```text',load('strict-properties.json')['diagnostics'][0]['file']+':'+str(load('strict-properties.json')['diagnostics'][0]['line'])+':'+str(load('strict-properties.json')['diagnostics'][0]['column'])+' TS2322',load('strict-properties.json')['diagnostics'][0]['message'],'```','','No annotation was fixed. Normal property `hereby dts` failed in build-services on this same error (task exit 1; tsc exit 2). It emitted fresh declaration intermediates, including the typescript entrypoint and compiler types. To obtain the actual API projection without weakening checking or modifying source, the unchanged official dts-services bundler command was run directly on those intermediates:','','```sh','node scripts/dtsBundler.mjs --entrypoint ./built/local/typescript/typescript.d.ts --output ./built/local/typescript.d.ts','```','','That projection succeeded. It is **not a successful property-road hereby dts build**. The property tsserverlibrary shim was not emitted because the full task stopped before dts-lssl. The exact **19,174-byte** [typescript.d.ts diff](property-typescript.d.ts.diff) is from the emitted intermediates and official bundler, not a predicted/manual declaration edit. It changes **34 public members** and retains previously internal call signatures inside the new property type literals: createStringLiteral **1→2**, createIdentifier **1→2**, createToken **11→12**. The @internal comments remain visible in that public projection; the bundler did not strip those nested signatures.','','The hybrid’s unmodified `hereby dts` passed. Both files compare byte for byte with baseline:','','| Bundle / road | Bytes | SHA-256 |','| --- | ---: | --- |']
